BlackVault — Internal Contract and Transaction Review

Prepared 13 September 2026 · Records through 12 September · Krista Dawn

Findings

The three supplied FUNTOKEN deployments are successful Sepolia deployments. All three contain identical runtime code and each minted 20 FUN. The wallet’s EIP-7702 delegation predates the token deployments: its activation is recorded on 30 August. The FUN creation transactions themselves are direct type-2 contract creations from that wallet.

This review also identified a successful 1-FUN self-transfer, two internal returns of Sepolia ETH missing from the normal-transaction CSV, the Safe contracts involved in those routes, and a recorded Safe threshold change from three signatures to two.

The two portfolio CSVs are duplicates for an address Kraken identifies as its kBTC token contract. Their displayed valuations cannot be treated as balances established in Krista’s personal wallet.

Review basis

Reviewed the supplied screenshots, four CSV files, the additional JPEG files carrying .crdownload extensions, and the FUNTOKEN image. Retrieved the relevant Sepolia explorer pages directly, compared the three runtime bytecodes, examined receipt logs and internal transfers, and matched the verified DeleGator source files to MetaMask’s v1.3.0 publication.

The separate Unconfirmed 2009.crdownload contains a Windows executable header rather than transaction data. It was identified by its bytes and was not executed or used as blockchain evidence.

BlackVault repository, website, and Vault AI progress statements draw on the existing project record. This review did not refresh repository or website implementation status. No contracts, wallets, repositories, wiki pages, or source-verification records were changed; no blockchain transaction was signed or submitted.

