3. What delegation adds, and where its authority ends

The account’s earlier authorization is confirmed by the 30 August type-4 transaction. The implementation’s verified principal sources exactly match MetaMask’s v1.3.0 files. Authorization receipt, Verified implementation.

Operation

Required account context

execute — single or batch

The EntryPoint or the executing account itself.

executeFromExecutor

The configured DelegationManager.

validateUserOp

The EntryPoint and delegated account context.

isValidSignature

Delegated account context; the recovered signer must equal the executing account.

enableDelegation / disableDelegation

Authorized account execution; manages a specific permission delegation.

addDeposit / withdrawDeposit

Concerns the executing account’s EntryPoint deposit, with the applicable call restrictions.

Connecting MetaMask to the shared implementation’s Etherscan page does not make that contract’s balances or account-dependent reads belong to the connected wallet. Account-specific queries should use the delegated wallet address and the implementation interface. The shared contract’s displayed native and token balances are separate.

Framework-owner functions, including the DelegationManager’s pause and ownership controls, are not rights granted by using the framework. Permission revocation and replacing the account’s EIP-7702 code delegation are also different operations. This review established the recorded implementation and historical executions; it did not enumerate every outstanding offchain permission signature. MetaMask account core, DelegationManager source, EIP-7702.

